{"timestamp": "2025-09-03T20:11:22.895069", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # Get the index of the goal item from the environment's cookbook\n  item_index = env.world.cookbook.index[item]\n  \n  # Find which workshop is required for crafting the item\n  # This would involve checking the recipe to see if a specific workshop is needed.\n  # For simplicity, let's assume that all recipes can be crafted at any workshop.\n  # In practice, you should check the recipe and find the appropriate workshop.\n  # Here we just pick one of the available workshops randomly for demonstration.\n  import random\n  workshop_index = random.choice(env.world.workshop_indices)\n  \n  # Actions to move to the chosen workshop\n  actions_to_workshop = []\n\n  # Get current position and direction of the agent\n  pos_x, pos_y = env._current_state.pos\n  dir_ = env._current_state.dir\n\n  # Define the target position as the position of the chosen workshop\n  # For simplicity, let's assume we know the coordinates of the workshop.\n  # In practice, you should find the actual coordinates of the workshop in the grid.\n  target_pos_x, target_pos_y = (0, 0)  # Replace with actual workshop coordinates\n\n  # Calculate the actions needed to move to the workshop\n  while pos_x != target_pos_x or pos_y != target_pos_y:\n      if pos_x < target_pos_x:\n          actions_to_workshop.append(env.world.cookbook.index[\"RIGHT\"])\n          pos_x += 1\n      elif pos_x > target_pos_x:\n          actions_to_workshop.append(env.world.cookbook.index[\"LEFT\"])\n          pos_x -= 1\n      \n      if pos_y < target_pos_y:\n          actions_to_workshop.append(env.world.cookbook.index[\"DOWN\"])\n          pos_y += 1\n      elif pos_y > target_pos_y:\n          actions_to_workshop.append(env.world.cookbook.index[\"UP\"])\n          pos_y -= 1\n\n  # Add the action to use the workshop (crafting the item)\n  actions_to_workshop.append(env.world.cookbook.index[\"USE\"])\n\n  return actions_to_workshop", "i